menu "T-Dongle-S3 device"
 config TDONGLE_SETUP_AP_OPEN
  bool "Open (passwordless) setup Wi-Fi access point"
  default y
  help
   The setup access point (TDongle-XXXXXX, shown on the screen) has no password, so anyone in range can open the setup page
   while setup is running (at most 10 minutes) and can add or delete saved Wi-Fi networks. This is the v0.1.x behaviour and an
   explicit owner decision: a phone joins it with one tap. The page can only change Wi-Fi networks; tailnets, the routing mode and
   diagnostics are never served on it. Turn it off to protect the access point with a random WPA2 password that the screen shows.
 config TDONGLE_WIFI_ROAMING_TAILNET
  bool "802.11k/v roaming assist in tailnet gateway mode"
  default n
  help
   The Wi-Fi bridge asks the access point to steer it to a better one (802.11k neighbour reports, 802.11v BSS transition requests), as
   v0.1.x did. The tailnet gateway does not by default: a roam briefly drops the Wi-Fi link and the tunnels with it, and its heap margin
   has not been measured with the feature on the board. Turn it on to measure.
endmenu
